{
  "id": 385177300,
  "iid": 19937,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "pcapng-netflix-custm: don't use sizeof for the tcpinfo option size.",
  "description": "struct nflx_tcpinfo has 64-bit integral type values in it, but the sum\nof the sizes of the elements plus internal padding is *not* a multiple\nof 8, so, on a platform on which 64-bit integral type values are aligned\non an 8-byte boundary - i.e., on all 64-bit platforms on which we run,\nprobably meaning on the majority of machines on which Wireshark is run\nthese days, especially given that we don't support 32-bit Windows or\nmacOS any more - it will have 4 bytes of unnamed padding at the end.\n\nThe custom option data in capture files does *not* necessarily include\nthe unnamed padding.\n\nInstead, explicitly define OPT_NFLX_TCPINFO_SIZE as the size consumed by\nthe *data* in the option - not padding added on 64-bit platforms - and\ncompare against *that* in a ws_assert().\n\nThis isn't an issue if asserts aren't compiled in, but will probably\nblow up on 64-bit platforms if options are compiled in.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2025-05-21T22:24:19.845Z",
  "updated_at": "2025-05-21T23:02:15.297Z",
